Z||000000||bpfiero||03-12-2001||01:02 PM||||I was driving around all day yesterday and all of a sudden I look at my temp. gauge and the damn needle fell off,  I just finished fixing all of the small crap on my car and now this.  So, can I just pop of  the dash and stick the needle back on, or do I have to buy a new cluster or just a gauge??? Or should I take this as a sign and get the white face gauges, and if so,  does anyone know were I can get them??? how much??? and how easy is it to put them in?????  hope you guys can help??? <BR>Brian <BR>86 GT N.Y. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cuz2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||My7Fieros||03-12-2001||01:24 PM||||Same thing happened to me. When I bought my gold 86 Gt it had fallen off (laying on the bottom of the guage). <BR>Take the dash apart and stick it back on...itll stay for another 15 years lol.<BR>After I took my dash apart, I let the car run long enough for the fan to kick on, then I placed the needle at the 235 mark (3rd line after the 220 mark).<BR>Just for the sake of knowing, each line on the temp guage represents 15 degrees from the 100 to the 220 side....then, each line represents only 5 degrees from the 220 to the 260 side.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://tgowens.com/My7Fieros_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||bpfiero||03-12-2001||01:29 PM||||so your gauge still works I take it??? <BR>thanks for the help!!!<BR> Brian<BR>||||reg||1
